# debian/halide-time-vote.policy -- time-source vote order (ch.05 section 29).
# Consumed by /usr/sbin/halide-time-vote (source: debian/scripts/halide-time-vote).
# Checked by tests/time-vote.sh: this file must name manual, NITZ and ntp.
#
# Vote order (highest trust first):
#   1. manual (user-manual pick, "Automatic" off): explicit human wins.
#      Stored with timestamp; stale-manual older than 30d warns "check
#      date/time" on TLS failures. Marks TIME_HOLD_MANUAL; NTP/NITZ/GNSS
#      are logged-only while manual holds.
#   2. ntp (chrony, endpoints in chrony.conf): default when Automatic on.
#      Fresh means synced within 24h with root dispersion <=1s (TIME_SYNC
#      journal line records stratum + dispersion per sync). NTP wins any
#      diverge; divergence >5min raises TIME_DIVERGE + telemetry counter
#      when opted-in, never a silent step.
#   3. NITZ (ModemManager ModemTime signal via ril-bridge): trusted for
#      timezone-hint + coarse sanity only. Never steps the clock more than
#      +-5min without NTP corroboration (base-station NITZ-spoofing threat,
#      ch.08 supply-chain table). When NTP is stale and NITZ is fresh, NITZ
#      steps with TIME_SOURCE=NITZ journal tag + re-sync NTP ASAP (metered
#      defer rule respected: data-cost honesty outranks sub-minute accuracy).
#   4. gnss (position-time): lowest weight for wall-clock. Aids SUPL
#      acquisition but 1s-class GNSS time never overrides NTP.
#      GNSS-week-rollover tested per SKU with fixture.
# Holdover: no fresh source -> hold last-known + CLOCK_HOLDOVER banner in
# Settings, per-SKU rtc-drift bounds shown (hw/<sku>/rtc-drift.md).
# RTC_SUSPECT: RTC reads pre-2026 or post-2040 -> ignore RTC, holdover +
# NTP ASAP + log (dead-coin-cell diagnosis, not mystery).
# Backward jumps >60s require container drain-quiesce: stop-container, step,
# restart-container (forward jumps apply immediately + TIME_SET broadcast).
